    {
        "id": "4761fea00c851552",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "a65f1d125d17f35a",
        "name": "Prerequisites \u2014 open me up first",
        "info": "This flow now talks to **lp700-server** over WebSocket, **not** USB-HID.\n\n1. Make sure lp700-server is running on your Pi (see the project README).\n2. Open the **`ws://lp700-server/ws`** node, edit the *websocket-client* config,\n   and set the URL to your Pi (default: `ws://raspberrypi.local:8089/ws`).\n3. Deploy. The *Parse WS frame* node's status pip turns green when heartbeats arrive.\n\nMultiple Node-RED instances and the embedded web client at\n`http://<pi-host>:8089/` can all read at once and any of them can issue control\nverbs \u2014 the server's single-writer queue serialises writes FIFO.\n",
        "x": 330,
        "y": 120,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "003125de085c5603",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "a65f1d125d17f35a",
        "name": "LP-500 / LP-700 HID DIRECT v1.2 - KD4Z",
        "info": "\nKD4Z    1.0 Proof of concept\nKD4Z    1.1 Added 3 step automatic scaling for power bargraphs.  100W - 500W - 1500W\nKD4Z    1.2 Added Peak hold functionality for the power label values\n            Added Channel and Range button actions\n            Changed automatic scaling to follow what the meter is doing.\n\n",
        "x": 200,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
